  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_011, acc 0.632) uses scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + concat in a multimodal multiprofile setup. We know multimodal helps (+4% over rna_only) and multiprofile helps substantially (+9% over singleprofile), but all experiments so far have used resnet50 as the image encoder. Uncertainty: We have zero evidence on whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) would further improve performance, which is a representation-level question with potentially large impact. This experiment (config_020: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is a clean single-variable change from config_011, isolating the image encoder effect. It is the best next experiment because the image representation quality is a more fundamental and potentially higher-impact design axis than fusion mechanism (concat vs weighted), and resolving whether the image modality can contribute more signal directly informs whether to invest further in image-side design choices."
}

